From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:53:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: MADEIRA_FEX_PAUSE=wait-os[:K[:U]], a PAUSE that
 blocks U us

yield-os (0084) gives a spinning thread's core to a thread already
waiting for it, and returns at once when there is none; under the power
clamp The Witcher 3's RenderThread still used about 70% of a core with
it. wait-os makes every K-th PAUSE of a thread a raw thread_switch Mach
trap (svc #0x80, x16 = -61) with MACH_PORT_NULL and
SWITCH_OPTION_DISPATCH_CONTENTION, libdispatch's contention back-off:
the kernel blocks the thread for U microseconds (assert_wait_timeout
in usec, osfmk/kern/syscall_subr.c) whether or not anything else is
runnable, so the core is free, or idle, for that long. The cost is up
to U us of extra latency when the awaited store lands mid-wait.

K is as for yield-os (default 128, 1 to 4095); U defaults to 50, 1 to
5000. x1 and x2, guest registers like x0, are saved in TMP3/TMP4
around the trap; the counters 0085 added time it the same way, so
[xp-pause] reports the waits. The disk-cache key already holds the
whole variable.

Linear: PLA-462
Class: feature
Evidence: tools/tests/test_fex_pause_yield_os.py
Offered-upstream: no; the switch is Playport's iOS host's
---
